      "id": "claim_02c3068dc89b46dd9b5ec03d15f664c5",
      "statement": "In gpuix a looping native animation costs the whole page per tick (per-replayed-root cost): one looping colour keyframe on one text took 7 ms a tick on 3000 nodes and about 60 ms on 12000 against 0.1 ms with nothing animating, so a page with a running loop idles at 37-45% CPU (the button page's native spinner takes its always-loading Saving button from 3.8% to 41%); the port has no workaround beyond pausing off-screen loops through culling.",
