    {
      "id": "claim_89779a13309844bc87111c1bea6a61ae",
      "statement": "Since gpuix poc b03d4e27, getBoundingClientRect, ResizeObserver, IntersectionObserver and onLayout return fractional 1/64 px values like Chrome (client* and scroll* stay integers), but gpuix still lays out an authored inset, padding or size on a whole device pixel (half toward zero), so a highlight placed from a measured rect can sit 0.5 px off its row; the port corrects this only for the fluid highlight by rounding rects like the source's offset* reads.",
